lesson: 88
title: So many each day
stars: 1
explain: A rate tells how much happens in one day, one week or one hour.
explain: To find how much in several days, multiply the amount for one day by the number of days.
explain: Reading 8 pages a day for 6 days makes 8 × 6 = 48 pages.
vars: a=name r=2..12 d=2..9 x=2..5
answer: r * d
exercise: {a} reads {r} pages a day. How many pages does {a} read in {d} days?
exercise: {a} saves {r} dollars each week. How much money does {a} save in {d} weeks?
exercise: A shop sells {r} bikes a week. How many bikes does it sell in {d} weeks?
exercise: {a} walks {r} km every day. How far does {a.he} walk in {d} days?
exercise: A machine makes {r} toys an hour. How many toys does it make in {d} hours?
exercise: {a} practises the piano for {r} minutes each day. How many minutes does {a.he} practise in {d} days?
test: In {d} weeks, how many dollars does {a} earn if {a.he} is paid {r} dollars a week?
test: For {d} days in a row {a} drinks {r} glasses of water a day. How many glasses is that?
test: A tap drips {r} drops every minute. How many drops fall in {d} minutes?
test: {a} is {x} years older than {a.his} brother and writes {r} lines a day. How many lines does {a.he} write in {d} days?
exercise: {a} earns {r} dollars a week for {d} weeks. How many dollars does {a.he} earn in all?
exercise: How many pages does {a} read in {d} days at {r} pages per day?
exercise: A bakery in Boston bakes {r} cakes every day. How many cakes does it bake in {d} days?
exercise: {a} swims {r} lengths each day in a pool in Sydney. How many lengths does {a.he} swim in {d} days?
exercise: A farm in Iowa sells {r} sacks of corn each week. How many sacks does it sell in {d} weeks?
exercise: {a} rides {r} km a day for {d} days in Ireland. How many km does {a.he} ride altogether?
exercise: {a} is {x} years older than {a.his} sister. {a.He} plants {r} flowers each day. How many flowers does {a.he} plant in {d} days?
exercise: A bus in Edinburgh makes {r} trips every day. How many trips does it make in {d} days?
test: For {d} hours a printer prints {r} pages each hour. How many pages does it print?
test: {a} gives {a.his} dog {r} biscuits per day. How many biscuits does the dog eat in {d} days?
test: A ferry in Wellington crosses the harbour {r} times a day. How many crossings does it make in {d} days?
test: {a} has {x} brothers and saves {r} dollars a week. How many dollars has {a.he} saved after {d} weeks?
test: A postman in Kent cycles {r} km a day. How many km does he cycle in {d} days?
test: {r} new books arrive at a library in Toronto every month. How many books arrive in {d} months?
exercise: {a} reads {r} pages a day, how many in {d} days
exercise: {a} saves {r} bucks a week, {d} weeks how much
exercise: {a} walks {r+1} km a day — no sorry, {r} km. how far in {d} days
exercise: shop sells {r} bikes a week, my mate says {d} weeks is {r*d-r}. nah, whats right
test: {d} days, {r} pages each. how many pages
test: {a} saves {r} dollars a week, got {x} piggy banks btw. how much in {d} weeks
test: {r} km every day for {d} days, {a} reckons {r*d+d}?? nah. how far really
exam: Whereas {a} reads {r} pages per day, determine the aggregate number of pages read over a period of {d} days.
exam: It is given that {a} deposits {r} dollars in savings each week. Ascertain the total sum saved over {d.words} weeks.
exam: Compute the total distance, in kilometres, travelled by a walker who covers {r} kilometres per day for {d} days.
exam: State the total number of pages completed by {a}, who completes {r.words} pages in each of {d.words} consecutive days.
exercise: Mum is "between jobs", so {a} gives her {r} dollars a week from {a.his} paper round. How many dollars does {a.he} give her in {d} weeks?
exercise: Since Grandad passed away, {a} leaves {r} flowers at his final resting place every week. How many flowers does {a.he} leave in {d} weeks?
test: the hamster carked it so now {a} gives the rabbit {r} carrots a day instead. {d} days, how many carrots. and don't say dunno
